---
const checkpoints = [
  ['Setup request', 'Coupa sends a cXML PunchoutSetupRequest when a buyer opens the supplier link. Match its buyer identity to the right Shopify catalog.'],
  ['Shopping and return', 'The buyer shops in the supplier store. PunchOut Central returns the cart as a cXML PunchoutOrderMessage to Coupa.'],
  ['Requisition and PO', 'Coupa adds the items to a requisition. Following buyer approval, Coupa can send a cXML OrderRequest. The approved PO is the trigger for the Shopify order.'],
  ['Invoice visibility', 'PunchOut Central links invoice activity to the buyer, PO and store order. Confirm the buyer’s separate invoice-delivery requirements during onboarding.']
];
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview"><div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
    <div class="page-hero__copy reveal"><span class="ey">Shopify Coupa PunchOut</span><h1>Connect Coupa buying to your Shopify supplier catalog.</h1><p class="lead">A Coupa buyer starts PunchOut in procurement, shops your configured Shopify catalog and returns a cart to a Coupa requisition. The Shopify order follows only after the approved purchase order arrives.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss a Coupa connection &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#flow">See the Coupa flow &darr;</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual logo-hero reveal"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>Buyer system</span><b>cXML PunchOut</b></div><div class="logo-hero__mark"><img src="/assets/logos/coupa.svg" alt="Coupa"></div><span class="logo-hero__status">PunchOut Central</span><h3>Coupa to Shopify</h3><p>Procurement on the buyer side; catalog and approved order on the supplier side.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="flow"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">Coupa workflow</span><h2>The returned cart becomes a requisition, not a store order.</h2><p class="lead">Coupa documents a cXML setup request, cart return, buyer approval and subsequent purchase order as separate events.</p></div>
    <div class="integration-flow reveal"><div class="integration-node"><strong>Coupa</strong><span>Buyer starts and approves</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node integration-node--accent"><strong>PunchOut Central</strong><span>Session and transaction</span></div><div class="integration-arrow">&rarr;</div><div class="integration-node"><strong>Shopify</strong><span>Supplier catalog and PO-backed order</span></div></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="details"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Onboarding</span><h2>Map Coupa’s buyer identity to the right store.</h2><p class="lead">Confirm the buyer’s cXML credentials, PunchOut endpoint, catalog access and PO routing with their Coupa administrator. PunchOut Central can serve more than one enterprise buyer from a Shopify store using buyer-specific settings.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">{checkpoints.map(([title, description], index) => <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Test before launch</span><h2>Test both the catalog session and the PO handoff.</h2><p class="lead">Use a Coupa test buyer to check the setup response and landing page, returned cart lines, requisition approval, approved PO and corresponding Shopify order. A successful launch alone does not prove the whole flow.</p></div>
    <div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/cxml/"><span>Protocol</span><h3>cXML PunchOut</h3><p>Review the session and cart messages used in the connection.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/integrations/shopify/"><span>Supplier side</span><h3>Shopify catalog</h3><p>See how the existing store serves buyer-specific access.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a><a class="related-card reveal" href="/how-it-works/"><span>Process</span><h3>Six transaction stages</h3><p>Follow cart, approval, PO, store order and invoice.</p><b>Explore &rarr;</b></a></div>
    <p><small>Buyer-side reference: <a href="https://docs.coupa.com/en/supplier-documentation/coupa-for-suppliers/supplier-integration-resources/cxml-examples/purchase-orders-and-punchouts/punchout-ordering">Coupa’s Punchout Ordering documentation</a>.</small></p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="sec soft" id="faq"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head center reveal"><span class="ey">FAQ</span><h2>Coupa integration questions</h2></div><div class="faq reveal">
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Does Coupa cart return place a Shopify order?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>No. Coupa adds returned items to a requisition. PunchOut Central creates the Shopify order after receiving the approved PO.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Which protocol does this Coupa flow use?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Coupa documents a cXML PunchOut flow. Confirm the exact buyer configuration and PO routing during setup; do not assume OCI for this connection.</p></div></div>
    <div class="fi"><button class="fq" type="button"><span>Is invoice delivery to Coupa automatic?</span><span class="plus">+</span></button><div class="fa"><p>Invoice activity is tracked by PunchOut Central. The buyer’s invoice-submission channel and requirements must be confirmed separately.</p></div></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">Bring your Coupa requirements</span><h2>Review the buyer setup and Shopify catalog together.</h2><p class="lead">Share the Coupa connection details and the store you want buyers to shop.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/integrations/procurement-systems/">Explore buyer systems</a></div></div></section>
</main>
